{%- comment -%}
  ISOLATION TEST — reachable at /?view=hero-test

  The homepage runs 47 scripts, Dawn's whole stylesheet, a fixed blurred
  background, a marquee and a sticky header. The hero is a fraction of that, yet
  every jitter fix so far has been aimed at the hero. This template renders the
  SAME section with none of the rest: no layout, no Dawn CSS or JS, no background
  layer, no header. Only the design tokens the section needs to lay out.

  If this scrolls smoothly on a phone and the real homepage does not, the hero is
  exonerated and the cause is in what this page leaves out. If this judders too,
  the cause is the section itself and the search narrows to one file.

  Delete once the question is settled.
{%- endcomment -%}
{% layout none %}<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>GummyChums — hero isolation test</title>
  {{ 'gc-tokens.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
  <style>
    body{margin:0;background:var(--c-bg,#FBF0E6);color:var(--c-ink,#2b2b2b)}
    .isolated-note{position:fixed;left:8px;top:8px;z-index:99999;background:rgba(0,0,0,.8);
      color:#fff;font:600 11px/1.4 system-ui;padding:5px 8px;border-radius:5px;pointer-events:none}
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <div class="isolated-note">ISOLATION TEST — hero only</div>
  {% section 'gc-home' %}
</body>
</html>
